<title>USA: Harmon Inds wins international contracts.</title>
<headline>Harmon Inds wins international contracts.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE SPRINGS, Mo. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmon Industries Inc, which supplies signal and train control equipment for railroads, said Monday it was awarded contracts totaling more than $1.7 million from new heavy-haul railroad customers in northern Brazil and southern Russia, and a current customer in Poland.</p>
<p>In Brazil, Harmon will upgrade the railroad's existing relay-based wayside signal system by designing and supplying new microprocessor-based interlocking systems.</p>
<p>In Poland, Harmon will supply new hot-bearing and hot-wheel defect-detection systems.</p>
<p>And in Russia, grade crossing equipment will be installed near the city of Baku, in Southern Russia, by an independent contractor.</p>
<p>Shares of Harmon were trading unchanged at 18-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
